# Jobs for the cluster resource manager:
#
#     python3 -m src.cluster plan --jobs experiments/cluster_jobs.example
#     python3 -m src.cluster run  --jobs experiments/cluster_jobs.example
#
# One job per line. `key=value` pairs before a standalone ` -- ` size the slot;
# everything after it is the command, run from the repo root with
# /home/danielco/miniconda3/bin first on PATH (bare python3 is the 3.8 sandbox).
# A line with no ` -- ` is a command with the defaults: cores=1 ram=4 gpu=0.
#
#   cores=N  cpus pinned to the job. It sees exactly these -- nproc reports N,
#            so n_jobs=-1 inside the job stays inside the slot.
#   ram=N    GB. Admission control only: summed and never overbooked in the
#            placement, but nothing stops a job that asked for less than it
#            uses. These hosts are cgroup v1, where a user unit's MemoryMax is
#            recorded and ignored.
#   gpu=N    cards. Needs --gpu-slots 1 (the strict 30% of a 2-card box is 0),
#            and only deepfive has a working driver.
#   name=X   unit name (nmr-X) and log name (logs/cluster/X.out). Must be
#            unique: `stop` addresses jobs by name.
#
# There is no queue and no dependency graph. `run` launches what fits NOW and
# prints what did not fit; it does not wait for capacity or order jobs against
# each other. Chain dependent steps inside one job's command, or run the second
# batch after the first finishes.

cores=8 ram=16 name=e120_ridge -- python3 -m src.run_forecast crypto ridge_glmnet --task regression --metric corr --cv-scheme rolling --data-version crypto/v2.0-fenccausal --run-name e120_ridge
cores=8 ram=16 name=e120_lgb -- python3 -m src.run_forecast crypto lgb_ktz --task regression --metric corr --cv-scheme rolling --data-version crypto/v2.0-fenccausal --run-name e120_lgb
cores=4 ram=8 name=e120_rf -- python3 -m src.run_forecast crypto rf_ktz --task regression --metric corr --cv-scheme rolling --data-version crypto/v2.0-fenccausal --run-name e120_rf
